# DESCRIPTION

Section 8 describes what runs the system: booting, services, devices, storage, installing and updating.

The machine's firmware starts Limine, which loads the kernel, its root task's modules and the boot image, checking each file against the hash in its configuration.
The root task starts svcd(8), which starts every service from its manifest in `/boot/svc` (see svc(6)), in order, and starts again those that exit when their manifest says so.
devmgr(8) starts the drivers; partd(8), fsd(4) and distd(8) bring up the disk, the system volume and the release it holds.

install(8) puts the system on a disk from an install medium; distd(8) applies a new release into a free slot, and rolls back to the one before.

